  "id": "COMPOUND:20369 - PROTEIN:5829",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential mechanism by which Tectoruside may interact with CHP-134, through a series of molecular targets. Tectoruside is implicated in targeting VMRC-LCP, which is a target of Cycloeudesmol and 7-O-Methylmangiferin, and all three compounds are linked to CHP-134. This indicates that Tectoruside may act through a shared pathway, possibly by inhibiting a common target that is subsequently involved in the activation of CHP-134. The scores from the paths suggest a moderate level of confidence in this relationship, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be elucidated. The presence of multiple compounds with similar targets supports the hypothesis that Tectoruside may exert its effects through a mechanism that involves the modulation of a key molecular node, which in turn influences CHP-134. The integration of these findings highlights the importance of understanding the functional role of VMRC-LCP and its downstream effects on CHP-134, which could provide insights into the therapeutic potential of Tectoruside and related compounds.",
